A||||51||FieroHeather||Any Fiero Passengers out there?||||5||
Z||000000||FieroHeather||05-23-2001||09:33 AM||||My boyfriend and I are in a disagreement as to where the Sub should be placed in his '87 GT fastback.  He wants to put it on the passanger side (MY SIDE) at my feet (which is going to be really crampy), or behind my seat (which will push me forward some and vibrate all of the phlem out of my chest when it is on!) LOL  We have discussed using up the center console for sub, but I want to hear from any passengers out there:<P>Why do the drivers NOT think about US PASSENGERS when modifying their beautiful cars???<P>*Sheesh*||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||05-23-2001||09:40 AM||||Hm, your boyfriend needs to learn a lesson!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>OK so I usually don't usually have passengers nor am I a passenger in my car ever, but I have a sub behind my drivers seat which pushes the seat all the way forward.  I am only 5' So I need it pushed all the way forward to reach my pedals, but I still dont think its too cramped.<P>I do agree that footwell is too cramped though. <P>And there's a lot of people from Barrie here...<P><BR>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||05-23-2001||09:42 AM||||With the right enclosure, you shouldn't feel cramped at all with the sub in the footwell. Prolly EVERYONE has seen a pic of my sub, so I won't post it unless requested, it doesn't take up anymore room from the passenger then the pedals take from the driver. We don't exactly get to stretch out either, ya know.<BR>At 6'6", however, I've got no problem fitting in the passenger side of my car.  <P>Now, the possibilty remains that you would have a complaint with any set-up, in that case, I suggest your man just get a set of headphones! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||05-23-2001||10:37 AM||||Ya I can barely get into Lisas car at 6'. I have an ole foggy question. Whats the whole point of the big 'sub' anyway, besides making all the loose parts of your car vibrate. I even turn the base way down with stock speakers to hear it with windows rolled down. That loud drumming actually gives me headaches and nausea. I couldnt imagine it for any period of time. Dont take this as a flame. If that what you like, thats cool. I just never heard an explanation. I dont even see any big base speakers at a live concert. They all looked the same at a Britney Spears concert I went to.<P><BR>(not a big music fan btw, rather listen to purring engines)||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||05-23-2001||11:22 AM||||Since stimpy didn't post his pic, I'll post mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/footwellsub_1_1.JPG"> <P>I haven't gotten any complaints. Just slide the seat back and there's plenty of room. How tall are you? If you're shorter than 6' this will be no problem at all. And I think behind the passenger seat is no good. Even though you <I>might</I> be able to get a little more foot room, the seat's gonna have to be all the way forward and the driver won't be able to see as good, looking to the right. (Did that make sense?)<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||10
Z||000005||AusFiero||05-23-2001||11:32 AM||||If your interested I am selling Centre Console Subwoofer kits now. First batch should be ready tomorrow when I go down to the joinery.<BR>Full details are in the mall at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/003406.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/003406.html</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/consolefront_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/consolefitted01_2.jpg"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Philphine||05-23-2001||11:45 AM||||you didn't mention how tall you are. i have an 8" sub in my footwell box and it's a little smaller than stimpy's and squoch's, but i don't think anything is too cramped if it dosen't come past that passenger side dead pedal. if i were doing mine again, or doing one for another car i'd probaly make mine as big as theirs with a 10". i'm 5'11".||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||05-23-2001||11:48 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B> Whats the whole point of the big 'sub' anyway, besides making all the loose parts of your car vibrate. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The more powerful a stereo system is, the less the speakers need to actually "work".  If you turn up a stock system all the way, and turned my system up 1/2 way, I guarantee that my system will be louder, not to mention have richer and fuller sound. I also assure you that the stock system will be much more tiring to the ears. Hence the nausea and headaches.<P>BTW, Britney Spears concert?! You're right, you are NOT a music fan!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>And since everyone else is playin show and tell...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=34099626&Sequence=5&res=high"> <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||elfiero||05-23-2001||11:58 AM||||I modified a stock sub housing to accept a<BR>6 1/2" kicker sub and used a 300W amp to<BR>power it-sounds great!-it "bangs"-thats what<BR>the guys(kids) at the car stereo shop say!||||reg||14
Z||000009||Songman||05-23-2001||12:03 PM||||I agree with you, Roger.. I don't get it either. Maybe I am just old...<P>I listen to country music anyway and we actually want to hear the words and stuff... hehe<P>To each his own, but in a two seater car I think you can make music sound really crappy when you have too much stuff in there. After all, you are playing it for you and your passenger, not the neighborhood...<P>I have mentioned before the kids who drive through my neighborhood at night and stop at the stop sign which is 40 yards from my house. I can hear their music clearly inside my house over the sound of my TV... In my old opinion, that is too much! heheh<P>Anyway... I'm sure you and your boyfriend will find somewhere to put it to make both of you happy... Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||05-23-2001||12:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I agree with you, Roger.. I don't get it either. Maybe I am just old...<P>I listen to country music anyway and we actually want to hear the words and stuff... hehe<P>To each his own, but in a two seater car I think you can make music sound really crappy when you have too much stuff in there. After all, you are playing it for you and your passenger, not the neighborhood...<P>I have mentioned before the kids who drive through my neighborhood at night and stop at the stop sign which is 40 yards from my house. I can hear their music clearly inside my house over the sound of my TV... In my old opinion, that is too much! heheh<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>To be sure, this is such thing as too much. There's a guy at work who has an IASCA show winner Ford Escort with something like 1800w. It's unreal. It can actually shift internal organs. It is incredibly clear at loud volume, thats why it wins, but it's way too much for listening enjoyment.  One 10" sub in a Fiero will have nowhere near that kind of impact.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B><BR>Anyway... I'm sure you and your boyfriend will find somewhere to put it to make both of you happy... Good luck.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HEY NOW, this is a family-oriented forum. None of that gutter talk. (Or do I just have  a dirty mind?)||||reg||1
Z||000011||tgowens||05-23-2001||12:29 PM||||you could always have him mount the sub-woofer like I mounted mine.........it takes up <I>no</I> space inside the car and <I>everybody</I> gets to hear the music!! (stimpy, can you make an enclosure for this one??)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sub_3_01.jpg"> ||||reg||1
