Z||000013||sqoach||05-23-2001||12:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>How did you guys do the footwell sub?  can I just BUY one outright?  I don't have that much time on my hands to spend building one...  <P>That's why FieroHeather has to put up with it behind her seat so far...<P>Maybe FieroBecky should get in on this one!<P><BR>FieroLisa -- yours is behind you?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Used fiberglass and resin. And fiberboard for mounting the sub on. stimpy is making and selling his enclosure. I could make another one too. But that one in the picture is using an 8" sub.||||reg||1
Z||000014||KnightRyder31||05-23-2001||12:42 PM||||LOL tgowens!!!!!<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000015||Raydar||05-23-2001||12:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I agree with you, Roger.. I don't get it either. Maybe I am just old...<P>I listen to country music anyway and we actually want to hear the words and stuff... hehe<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't say that. I MUST be older than you. <P>Just different tastes. <BR>Rock (or rap or alternative or whatever) is designed to be played loud. Half of the fun of listening to rock is feeling the music. <P>Country music is just "built" differently. Most country music can be enjoyed without it having to shake the room.   <P>BTW... I'm 44 and I still like to "feel" my music. <BR>I've got 10 speakers and about 320 watts of amplification in my extended cab Sonoma. <BR>People ask "Why so much power?" <BR>I answer "I can feel the music, and I can roll down the window and the sound doesn't suffer at all."<BR>Other people ask "Why not more power?"<BR>I answer "The pain sets in before the distortion does. That's all I need."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And no. I don't annoy people with it. <BR>I don't drive through neighborhoods with music blaring. It annoys me to be in the house and have to listen to other people's music, as they drive by. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000016||grinthock||05-23-2001||12:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>With the right enclosure, you shouldn't feel cramped at all with the sub in the footwell. Prolly EVERYONE has seen a pic of my sub, so I won't post it unless requested, it doesn't take up anymore room from the passenger then the pedals take from the driver. We don't exactly get to stretch out either, ya know.<BR>At 6'6", however, I've got no problem fitting in the passenger side of my car.  <P>Now, the possibilty remains that you would have a complaint with any set-up, in that case, I suggest your man just get a set of headphones!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok I am a loser -- Post it anyway how much do you want for them? What size a sub do they take?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||stimpy||05-23-2001||01:01 PM||||Talk about coincidence. While you're typing that post, I'm sending you email. Howabout dat?<P>Anyhow, that's my box in the car w/ the tan interior. It takes a 10" sub, but I also imagine one could put 2 8" subs. Cost is competitive with other options. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Taijiguy||05-23-2001||01:08 PM||||There's a difference between obnoxious, and accurate. Having a huge sub (or a <I>bunch</I> of huge subs doesn't equal accurate sound reproduction. Evidence of this lies in that most people with huge stereos pay no attention to one of the primary ratings of an amp: slew rate. The best stereo I ever heard was the one I had in my kit car many years ago. 4 6x9 coax speakers, with 2 sony 100 watt amps. They had the fastest slew rate imaginable. The result was enough power  to provide good strong bass, with a fast enough response to give the cleanest sounding snare drums and precise reproduction of guitar picking, down to every detail. And it was PLENTY loud, when the drum part to "Time Loves A Hero" (Little Feat) would start, you'd think you had your head stuck inside the snare drum.  God I miss that stereo ::sniff::||||reg||1
Z||000019||grinthock||05-23-2001||01:10 PM||||I got the email, price sounds good, it's about what I expected, I will email you when I am ready...  Now I am considering both a footwell and a centre console sub... IN THE FUTURE probably go with one of them for now....   I will email off list when ready....  THe cost is ok, but cash is kinda right right now, I need rim/tires first||||reg||1
